  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather will persist through tonight, then \nchances for rain return Sunday through Monday.\n\nBroads surface high pressure across eastern Ontario and Quebec \nwill remain in place today before drifting east Sunday. \nSubsidence and dry air associated with the high will continue to\nsupport dry weather through tonight, although there will be more\nhigh clouds than the past few days.\n\nMeanwhile, an unseasonably strong coastal low off the Delmarva will \nremain in place today while maturing and occluding. The coastal low \nwill then complete a cyclonic loop to the south of Long Island \ntonight through Sunday, nearing the Jersey shore by late Sunday and \nSunday night. The westward drift in the position of the vertically \nstacked low will advect Atlantic moisture westward across NY/PA, \nwith thickening and lowering clouds. The first chance of showers \nwill reach central NY Sunday morning, then progress gradually \nwestward as an inverted trough axis north of the low center rotates \nwestward. Showers may reach the Genesee Valley and western Finger \nLakes by early to mid afternoon. Far western New York should stay\ndry most of Sunday, although a few light showers may arrive by \nlate afternoon or evening given the westward trend in recent \nmodel guidance.\n\nThe coastal low is then forecast to slowly meander northeast along \nthe New England coast Sunday night through Tuesday, weakening with \ntime. The greatest rain chances and greatest western extent of the \nrain shield will be Sunday night, with showers then gradually \ntapering off and ending from west to east late Sunday night\nthrough Monday as the low weakens and moves northeast.",
